  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want the menu that opens from a tap on a member's avatar or pseudo to be anchored on that pseudo, like the message's « + » menu (#924), so that it appears where I tapped and not in the top-left corner of the screen.\n\n### Observed (operator, iPhone, 2026-11-16)\n\n- A tap on the avatar or pseudo shows the author menu « Post de <pseudo> » (Profil, MP, Blacklist, Whitelist) as a panel in the **top-left corner**, over the title bar, far from the tapped post.\n- The « + » menu of the same post opens **anchored at the tapped spot**, as the system's horizontal callout (Citer, Citer □, Link, Alerter).\n- Screenshots kept locally by the operator (they show member pseudos, so they are not attached).\n\n### Wanted\n\n- The author menu is anchored on the tapped pseudo or avatar (`ReaderMessageMenuAnchor`, as the « + » menu does), in the same visual family.\n- A vertical list may stay if the system's callout cannot hold four items with icons. It must sit next to the pseudo.\n\n### Note\n\n#652 / #953 (merged in cd049542) makes the tap open the **profile directly** when the post has a profile link. The author menu then shows only for a post without one. If the operator's build already includes cd049542 and the menu still shows for a normal post, that is a second bug, to check in the same PR.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The author menu opens anchored at the tapped pseudo or avatar, never in the corner.\n- [ ] A test of the anchor rect that the menu receives (from the bridge message's coordinates) fails without the change.\n- [ ] Device check in the general review.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
